{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"invalid-index-comparison-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalid index comparison review"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production/test head: the commit that adds this record.\nThis record is a documentation-only follow-up to that head."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"law-and-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Law and boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A custom index comparator must return a number that is not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":". A comparator\nthat returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":", a boolean, or any non-number cannot order the index's\nstorage. Per "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" (\"Separate Valid Edge Cases from Contract\nContradictions\"), a broken comparator is a caller programming error, so the\nindex crashes: the operation that receives an invalid result throws. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":"\nvalues ordered by the default comparator remain valid and supported."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"makeCheckedComparator"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src/utils/comparison.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" wraps a\nuser-supplied "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compareFn"},{"type":"text","value":" and throws a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TypeError"},{"type":"text","value":" on any result that is not a\nnon-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" number. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BaseIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" builds every index's comparator through it, so\nboth "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BasicIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BTreeIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" share one enforcement point. Because the\ncomparator now guarantees a valid order, the vendored B+ tree no longer needs\nits own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":"/invalid-result branch, and the post-split child placement follows\nthe already-known insertion index instead of a redundant comparison. Net\nproduction code shrinks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The index owner ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/tests/index-update.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":") states the\nrefinement law: for each index type, comparator, accepted numeric prefix, and\nprobe operation, the operation throws exactly when it receives an invalid\ncomparison result, and never when every comparison it makes is valid. The\nmodel counts invalid results independently of the production check. An empty\nprefix is included: the first write compares nothing and must succeed, and the\nnext comparing operation must throw. The BTree Map owner\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/tests/btree-map-oracle.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":") keeps two split histories that\nprove split placement does not consult a post-mutation comparison."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A rejected index "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"add"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"remove"},{"type":"text","value":" throws before it changes the index, so the\nindex still refines its accepted rows. Index "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"build"},{"type":"text","value":" are not\natomic. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" builds before it registers the index, so a failed build\nnever reaches a collection."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"collection-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Collection boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An external review showed that the first version of this change was worse than\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" at the Collection boundary. The Collection writes rows before it\nupdates indexes and publishes change events. An index throw between those\nsteps left rows that subscribers were never told about, while the collection\nstayed usable and reported the write as failed. That is the partial success\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" forbids. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" stored and published those rows; only its index\norder was wrong."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The repair crashes the collection. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionIndexesManager.updateIndexes"},{"type":"text","value":"\ncalls the existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lifecycle.markError"},{"type":"text","value":" and rethrows. The collection status\nbecomes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":", and the next mutation throws "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionInErrorStateError"},{"type":"text","value":".\nNo recovery path, generation, or rollback is added. The index owner states\nthis law for both index types and both write paths (optimistic insert and sync\ncommit)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remaining limits:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sync source can still begin and commit writes on a collection in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":"\nstate. Those rows are stored but not published. This is existing\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markError"},{"type":"text","value":" behavior for any crashed collection, not specific to comparators."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A user who relied on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"'s silently misordered index now gets a crashed\ncollection at the first invalid comparison. The changeset states this."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparator transitivity is not validated."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"conformance-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conformance evidence"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The index comparator contract and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" fail-fast policy supply the law; the limits above bound it."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-002"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The refinement model counts invalid comparator results with its own recording wrapper. It does not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"makeCheckedComparator"},{"type":"text","value":" or any production classifier."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-003"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The opening comment states the law and limits; the probe/comparator/prefix tables supply inputs; public "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"add"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lookup"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"take"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"build"},{"type":"text","value":" drive production; the recording step judges throw-vs-success."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-004"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bounded enumeration crosses two index types, three comparators, seven probe operations, and seven prefixes including the empty prefix. The empty prefix reconstructs the first-write-never-compares case. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signed infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" comparator is the marginal valid case; it must never throw."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-005"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Public index entry points execute, and the Collection cells drive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.insert"},{"type":"text","value":" and a sync "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit"},{"type":"text","value":". Observations: throw vs. success, accepted-row refinement after a rejected add/remove, and collection status plus the next mutation after a rejected write."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-006"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On unmodified "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":", the BasicIndex law and the reported-string case fail (85 cases). Mutants that leave either index's comparator unchecked, that reject only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" (accepting booleans), or that also reject infinite results each fail at the intended checkpoint. All were classified as assertion failures."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-007"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are bounded enumerations, not an important generated property; no fixed/random campaign parity is required. The package's existing generated index campaign is unchanged."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-008"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No stateful reference model is introduced; the check recomputes throw-vs-success per operation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-009"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepted rows and index operations retain existing vocabulary."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-010"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checks are synchronous and retain no resources."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-011"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both index types run through the same law, distinguishing an index-type-specific fault from a shared one."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-012"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This record names the reviewed head and each applicable outcome. It makes no universal bug-class closure claim; the sync-writes-after-crash limit above stays open."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutant-kills-recorded-at-review-time","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant kills (recorded at review time)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vitest run tests/index-update.property.test.ts -t \"invalid comparator results|NaN keys|reported string\""},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" production (no check)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"85 assertion failures (all BasicIndex; BTreeIndex passed the law but not the error class)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BTreeIndex comparator unchecked"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"84 assertion failures."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BasicIndex comparator unchecked"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"84 assertion failures."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check rejects only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":", accepts booleans"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"84 assertion failures."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check also rejects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"±Infinity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"82 assertion failures (the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signed infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" valid control now throws)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shipped fix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0 failures."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Collection and atomicity cells, run with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-t \"invalid comparator|rejected remove\""},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PR head before this repair"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"12 assertion failures: 4 Collection cells (status stayed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ready"},{"type":"text","value":"), 6 BasicIndex add cells, 2 remove cells."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateIndexes"},{"type":"text","value":" rethrows without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markError"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4 assertion failures (Collection cells)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BasicIndex add writes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"valueMap"},{"type":"text","value":" before its sorted search"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6 assertion failures."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BTreeIndex remove changes maps before the tree delete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 assertion failure."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shipped fix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0 failures."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" suite passes: 223 files, 7,429 tests, no type errors.\nProduction code is net negative against the merge base. Tests and this record\ngrow separately."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"invalid-index-comparison-review","text":"Invalid index comparison review","level":1},{"id":"law-and-boundary","text":"Law and boundary","level":2},{"id":"collection-boundary","text":"Collection boundary","level":3},{"id":"conformance-evidence","text":"Conformance evidence","level":2},{"id":"mutant-kills-recorded-at-review-time","text":"Mutant kills (recorded at review time)","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Invalid index comparison review\n\nProduction/test head: the commit that adds this record.\nThis record is a documentation-only follow-up to that head.\n\n## Law and boundary\n\nA custom index comparator must return a number that is not `NaN`. A comparator\nthat returns `NaN`, a boolean, or any non-number cannot order the index's\nstorage. Per `AGENTS.md` (\"Separate Valid Edge Cases from Contract\nContradictions\"), a broken comparator is a caller programming error, so the\nindex crashes: the operation that receives an invalid result throws. `NaN`\nvalues ordered by the default comparator remain valid and supported.\n\n`makeCheckedComparator` in `packages/db/src/utils/comparison.ts` wraps a\nuser-supplied `compareFn` and throws a `TypeError` on any result that is not a\nnon-`NaN` number. `BaseIndex` builds every index's comparator through it, so\nboth `BasicIndex` and `BTreeIndex` share one enforcement point. Because the\ncomparator now guarantees a valid order, the vendored B+ tree no longer needs\nits own `NaN`/invalid-result branch, and the post-split child placement follows\nthe already-known insertion index instead of a redundant comparison. Net\nproduction code shrinks.\n\nThe index owner (`packages/db/tests/index-update.property.test.ts`) states the\nrefinement law: for each index type, comparator, accepted numeric prefix, and\nprobe operation, the operation throws exactly when it receives an invalid\ncomparison result, and never when every comparison it makes is valid. The\nmodel counts invalid results independently of the production check. An empty\nprefix is included: the first write compares nothing and must succeed, and the\nnext comparing operation must throw. The BTree Map owner\n(`packages/db/tests/btree-map-oracle.test.ts`) keeps two split histories that\nprove split placement does not consult a post-mutation comparison.\n\nA rejected index `add` or `remove` throws before it changes the index, so the\nindex still refines its accepted rows. Index `update` and `build` are not\natomic. `createIndex` builds before it registers the index, so a failed build\nnever reaches a collection.\n\n### Collection boundary\n\nAn external review showed that the first version of this change was worse than\n`main` at the Collection boundary. The Collection writes rows before it\nupdates indexes and publishes change events. An index throw between those\nsteps left rows that subscribers were never told about, while the collection\nstayed usable and reported the write as failed. That is the partial success\n`AGENTS.md` forbids. `main` stored and published those rows; only its index\norder was wrong.\n\nThe repair crashes the collection. `CollectionIndexesManager.updateIndexes`\ncalls the existing `lifecycle.markError` and rethrows. The collection status\nbecomes `error`, and the next mutation throws `CollectionInErrorStateError`.\nNo recovery path, generation, or rollback is added. The index owner states\nthis law for both index types and both write paths (optimistic insert and sync\ncommit).\n\nRemaining limits:\n\n- A sync source can still begin and commit writes on a collection in `error`\n  state. Those rows are stored but not published. This is existing\n  `markError` behavior for any crashed collection, not specific to comparators.\n- A user who relied on `main`'s silently misordered index now gets a crashed\n  collection at the first invalid comparison. The changeset states this.\n- Comparator transitivity is not validated.\n\n## Conformance evidence\n\n| Requirement | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | The index comparator contract and `AGENTS.md` fail-fast policy supply the law; the limits above bound it. |\n| ORC-002 | The refinement model counts invalid comparator results with its own recording wrapper. It does not call `makeCheckedComparator` or any production classifier. |\n| ORC-003 | The opening comment states the law and limits; the probe/comparator/prefix tables supply inputs; public `add`/`update`/`lookup`/`take`/`build` drive production; the recording step judges throw-vs-success. |\n| ORC-004 | Bounded enumeration crosses two index types, three comparators, seven probe operations, and seven prefixes including the empty prefix. The empty prefix reconstructs the first-write-never-compares case. The `signed infinity` comparator is the marginal valid case; it must never throw. |\n| ORC-005 | Public index entry points execute, and the Collection cells drive `collection.insert` and a sync `commit`. Observations: throw vs. success, accepted-row refinement after a rejected add/remove, and collection status plus the next mutation after a rejected write. |\n| ORC-006 | On unmodified `origin/main`, the BasicIndex law and the reported-string case fail (85 cases). Mutants that leave either index's comparator unchecked, that reject only `NaN` (accepting booleans), or that also reject infinite results each fail at the intended checkpoint. All were classified as assertion failures. |\n| ORC-007 | These are bounded enumerations, not an important generated property; no fixed/random campaign parity is required. The package's existing generated index campaign is unchanged. |\n| ORC-008 | No stateful reference model is introduced; the check recomputes throw-vs-success per operation. |\n| ORC-009 | Accepted rows and index operations retain existing vocabulary. |\n| ORC-010 | Checks are synchronous and retain no resources. |\n| ORC-011 | Both index types run through the same law, distinguishing an index-type-specific fault from a shared one. |\n| ORC-012 | This record names the reviewed head and each applicable outcome. It makes no universal bug-class closure claim; the sync-writes-after-crash limit above stays open. |\n\n## Mutant kills (recorded at review time)\n\nRun: `vitest run tests/index-update.property.test.ts -t \"invalid comparator results|NaN keys|reported string\"`.\n\n| Mutant | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `origin/main` production (no check) | 85 assertion failures (all BasicIndex; BTreeIndex passed the law but not the error class). |\n| BTreeIndex comparator unchecked | 84 assertion failures. |\n| BasicIndex comparator unchecked | 84 assertion failures. |\n| Check rejects only `NaN`, accepts booleans | 84 assertion failures. |\n| Check also rejects `±Infinity` | 82 assertion failures (the `signed infinity` valid control now throws). |\n| Shipped fix | 0 failures. |\n\nCollection and atomicity cells, run with `-t \"invalid comparator|rejected remove\"`:\n\n| Mutant | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| PR head before this repair | 12 assertion failures: 4 Collection cells (status stayed `ready`), 6 BasicIndex add cells, 2 remove cells. |\n| `updateIndexes` rethrows without `markError` | 4 assertion failures (Collection cells). |\n| BasicIndex add writes `valueMap` before its sorted search | 6 assertion failures. |\n| BTreeIndex remove changes maps before the tree delete | 1 assertion failure. |\n| Shipped fix | 0 failures. |\n\nThe full `@tanstack/db` suite passes: 223 files, 7,429 tests, no type errors.\nProduction code is net negative against the merge base. Tests and this record\ngrow separately.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Invalid index comparison review\n\nProduction/test head: the commit that adds this record.\nThis record is a documentation-only follow-up to that head.\n\n## Law and boundary\n\nA custom index comparator must return a number that is not `NaN`. A comparator\nthat returns `NaN`, a boolean, or any non-number cannot order the index's\nstorage. Per `AGENTS.md` (\"Separate Valid Edge Cases from Contract\nContradictions\"), a broken comparator is a caller programming error, so the\nindex crashes: the operation that receives an invalid result throws. `NaN`\nvalues ordered by the default comparator remain valid and supported.\n\n`makeCheckedComparator` in `packages/db/src/utils/comparison.ts` wraps a\nuser-supplied `compareFn` and throws a `TypeError` on any result that is not a\nnon-`NaN` number. `BaseIndex` builds every index's comparator through it, so\nboth `BasicIndex` and `BTreeIndex` share one enforcement point. Because the\ncomparator now guarantees a valid order, the vendored B+ tree no longer needs\nits own `NaN`/invalid-result branch, and the post-split child placement follows\nthe already-known insertion index instead of a redundant comparison. Net\nproduction code shrinks.\n\nThe index owner (`packages/db/tests/index-update.property.test.ts`) states the\nrefinement law: for each index type, comparator, accepted numeric prefix, and\nprobe operation, the operation throws exactly when it receives an invalid\ncomparison result, and never when every comparison it makes is valid. The\nmodel counts invalid results independently of the production check. An empty\nprefix is included: the first write compares nothing and must succeed, and the\nnext comparing operation must throw. The BTree Map owner\n(`packages/db/tests/btree-map-oracle.test.ts`) keeps two split histories that\nprove split placement does not consult a post-mutation comparison.\n\nA rejected index `add` or `remove` throws before it changes the index, so the\nindex still refines its accepted rows. Index `update` and `build` are not\natomic. `createIndex` builds before it registers the index, so a failed build\nnever reaches a collection.\n\n### Collection boundary\n\nAn external review showed that the first version of this change was worse than\n`main` at the Collection boundary. The Collection writes rows before it\nupdates indexes and publishes change events. An index throw between those\nsteps left rows that subscribers were never told about, while the collection\nstayed usable and reported the write as failed. That is the partial success\n`AGENTS.md` forbids. `main` stored and published those rows; only its index\norder was wrong.\n\nThe repair crashes the collection. `CollectionIndexesManager.updateIndexes`\ncalls the existing `lifecycle.markError` and rethrows. The collection status\nbecomes `error`, and the next mutation throws `CollectionInErrorStateError`.\nNo recovery path, generation, or rollback is added. The index owner states\nthis law for both index types and both write paths (optimistic insert and sync\ncommit).\n\nRemaining limits:\n\n- A sync source can still begin and commit writes on a collection in `error`\n  state. Those rows are stored but not published. This is existing\n  `markError` behavior for any crashed collection, not specific to comparators.\n- A user who relied on `main`'s silently misordered index now gets a crashed\n  collection at the first invalid comparison. The changeset states this.\n- Comparator transitivity is not validated.\n\n## Conformance evidence\n\n| Requirement | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | The index comparator contract and `AGENTS.md` fail-fast policy supply the law; the limits above bound it. |\n| ORC-002 | The refinement model counts invalid comparator results with its own recording wrapper. It does not call `makeCheckedComparator` or any production classifier. |\n| ORC-003 | The opening comment states the law and limits; the probe/comparator/prefix tables supply inputs; public `add`/`update`/`lookup`/`take`/`build` drive production; the recording step judges throw-vs-success. |\n| ORC-004 | Bounded enumeration crosses two index types, three comparators, seven probe operations, and seven prefixes including the empty prefix. The empty prefix reconstructs the first-write-never-compares case. The `signed infinity` comparator is the marginal valid case; it must never throw. |\n| ORC-005 | Public index entry points execute, and the Collection cells drive `collection.insert` and a sync `commit`. Observations: throw vs. success, accepted-row refinement after a rejected add/remove, and collection status plus the next mutation after a rejected write. |\n| ORC-006 | On unmodified `origin/main`, the BasicIndex law and the reported-string case fail (85 cases). Mutants that leave either index's comparator unchecked, that reject only `NaN` (accepting booleans), or that also reject infinite results each fail at the intended checkpoint. All were classified as assertion failures. |\n| ORC-007 | These are bounded enumerations, not an important generated property; no fixed/random campaign parity is required. The package's existing generated index campaign is unchanged. |\n| ORC-008 | No stateful reference model is introduced; the check recomputes throw-vs-success per operation. |\n| ORC-009 | Accepted rows and index operations retain existing vocabulary. |\n| ORC-010 | Checks are synchronous and retain no resources. |\n| ORC-011 | Both index types run through the same law, distinguishing an index-type-specific fault from a shared one. |\n| ORC-012 | This record names the reviewed head and each applicable outcome. It makes no universal bug-class closure claim; the sync-writes-after-crash limit above stays open. |\n\n## Mutant kills (recorded at review time)\n\nRun: `vitest run tests/index-update.property.test.ts -t \"invalid comparator results|NaN keys|reported string\"`.\n\n| Mutant | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `origin/main` production (no check) | 85 assertion failures (all BasicIndex; BTreeIndex passed the law but not the error class). |\n| BTreeIndex comparator unchecked | 84 assertion failures. |\n| BasicIndex comparator unchecked | 84 assertion failures. |\n| Check rejects only `NaN`, accepts booleans | 84 assertion failures. |\n| Check also rejects `±Infinity` | 82 assertion failures (the `signed infinity` valid control now throws). |\n| Shipped fix | 0 failures. |\n\nCollection and atomicity cells, run with `-t \"invalid comparator|rejected remove\"`:\n\n| Mutant | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| PR head before this repair | 12 assertion failures: 4 Collection cells (status stayed `ready`), 6 BasicIndex add cells, 2 remove cells. |\n| `updateIndexes` rethrows without `markError` | 4 assertion failures (Collection cells). |\n| BasicIndex add writes `valueMap` before its sorted search | 6 assertion failures. |\n| BTreeIndex remove changes maps before the tree delete | 1 assertion failure. |\n| Shipped fix | 0 failures. |\n\nThe full `@tanstack/db` suite passes: 223 files, 7,429 tests, no type errors.\nProduction code is net negative against the merge base. Tests and this record\ngrow separately.\n"}
